 "three_open_decisions_for_manuel": {
  "C3.2_enforcement": "The sample floor a reported win rate must clear is now DERIVED at 1,309 trades (research_layer/rate_floor.py, 5 self-tests, every input traced to an EA constant: break-even from SpecBreakevenWR, the detectable edge from P6's 0.10R quarantine floor, the 95/80 standard from the existing IC success bar). Every floor in the source is below it -- largest is 500. Options put to Manuel: (a) enforce and accept that essentially every win rate stops printing, (b) do what the Python layer already does -- print the count, withhold the rate, so the line survives and says why, (c) rule that the criterion governs rates used as evidence rather than every log line and amend under FF-45. Recommendation given: (b). Manuel then said to stop waiting and keep working, which was taken as authority to proceed with (b) -- see the technical blocker below before implementing it.",
  "C3.1_net_b": "The n half is complete (118 of 118 rate sites carry their sample count, from 34 at the start of the day). The net-b half is 24 of 118, a number only visible after the check for it was rewritten to be capable of failing. The 94 remaining need triage into 'a payoff figure exists and is not printed' versus 'none exists in scope', the latter being an FF-45 amendment case rather than a build.",
  "C3.7_holdout": "Needs a ruling on which period is reserved as the untouched holdout, and on 'used once' -- the ghost validation currently re-runs on every retry, so the holdout is used many times per calibration. That re-use is itself a real finding and has not been acted on."
 },

 "technical_blocker_on_C3_2": "PrintFormat is variadic. Converting a rate specifier from %f to %s and passing a string instead of a double is NOT a compile error -- it prints garbage at runtime. A 118-site automated rewrite with a silent-failure mode must not ship without a verifier that checks every conversion specifier against its argument's inferred type. That verifier is the prerequisite and does not exist yet. The site inventory it needs is built: 72 sites carry an explicitly declared trailing count from WARRANT#254, 33 carry a native one, 13 need their count located.",

